<title>UK: UK PSBR 4.53 bln stg in August.</title>
<headline>UK PSBR 4.53 bln stg in August.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK public sector borrowing requirement data for August. Deficits unless noted (rep).</p>
<p> PSBR (in bln stg)		 AUG	APR-AUG     APR-AUG</p>
<p>						    1995/96     1994/95</p>
<p> Public sector		    4.533     13.370	16.717</p>
<p> Central government	     5.761     12.999	17.424</p>
<p> Central government own acct  5.242     13.403	17.051</p>
<p> Local Authority		    356rep     841	   391</p>
<p>  from central govt		 494	  867	   152</p>
<p> General Government	     4.911     12.973	17.663</p>
<p> Public Corporation		 353rep     874rep   725rep</p>
<p>   from central govt		 25	1.271rep	221</p>
<p>NOTE -F/cast was for a 4.1 bln stg Aug PSBR.Rep=repayment GOVERNMENT RECEIPTS</p>
<p> Central govt total receipts   17.992  100.538     94.538</p>
<p> Inland Revenue receipts	  5.807   36.450     34.820</p>
<p>  of which income tax	     4.676   27.820     27.495</p>
<p>  corporation tax		     345    6.520	5.651</p>
<p> Customs and excise		 6.858   33.905     31.512</p>
<p>  of which VAT			3.294   20.180     18.385</p>
<p> Social security		    3.243   18.656     17.941</p>
<p> Interest				 435    2.598	2.572</p>
<p> Other				  1.649    8.929	7.693</p>
<p>CENTRAL GOVERNMENT OUTLAYS</p>
<p>  Total				23.234  113.941    111.589</p>
<p>   of which Interest		2.053   10.127	8.977</p>
<p>   Net departmental outlays    21.617  106.494    102.614</p>
<p>NOTE- Privatisation proceeds in August were 436 million stg, compared with costs of one million in August last year.</p>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) said August's privatisation proceeds resulted mainly from the sale of British Telecommunications Plc loan stocks.</p>
<p>September's PSBR will include privatisation proceeds of about 1.0 billion stg. Of this, 200 million stg will be from the sale of National Power, PowerGen and Southern Electric shares. About 800 million stg is expected from the final call on GENCO2, the ONS said.</p>
